# width: 120
# height: 40
# The launcher dock's edge grip (src/ui/edge_grip.zig): `⋯` at the
# middle of the SCREEN's last row — the `:` line's row, cells 58..60
# with the glyph on 59 at 120 columns. The grip marks the EDGE, which
# is where a hand goes to summon a thing, so it sits on that row under
# both placements; under the default `ui.dock.placement = .inner` the
# strip it summons paints two rows up, above the statusline, so the `:`
# line's row keeps its own job while the strip is out.
#
# `edge_grip_dock_outer.test` is the other placement, where the strip
# lands on the grip's own row and the `:` line has to take it back.
#
# The bar and the columns ship `.always`, so the only grip on this
# screen is the dock's.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
# `auto_hide`, as mnml ships: nothing is drawn, and the grip says where.
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect screen contains "⋯"
# Dwelling on it reveals the strip, because the grip is INSIDE the
# dock's hover zone and not a second way in.
hover 59 39
wait 600
expect screen contains "New terminal"
# Away: the strip goes and the grip comes back.
hover 60 10
wait 800
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect screen contains "⋯"

# ── the revealed strip lands on the EDITOR's last row, not this one ──
# The `:` line's row goes on answering for itself while the strip is
# out: a click there opens the line, which under `.outer` — where the
# strip paints over that row — it cannot (`edge_grip_dock_outer.test`
# has the other half of this pair).
hover 30 39
wait 600
expect screen contains "New terminal"
click 110 39
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
key esc
hover 60 10
wait 800
expect screen lacks "New terminal"

# ── an open `:` line takes the grip's cells back ──
# The grip is on that row whichever placement is in force, so it stands
# down rather than painting over what is being typed. The strip itself
# is above the statusline and covers nothing of the line, so it is NOT
# refused: the dwell still brings it out while the line takes keys.
key ctrl+;
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
expect screen lacks "⋯"
hover 59 39
wait 600
expect screen contains "New terminal"
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
key esc
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":false"
hover 60 10
wait 800
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect screen contains "⋯"

# ── a click on the grip pins, and never opens the `:` line ──
# The grip's hit is registered after the row's own and wins its cells.
click 59 39
expect screen contains "dock pinned"
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":false"
expect screen contains "New terminal"
expect screen lacks "⋯"

# ── pinned, the strip is the editor area's last row and the `:` line
#    is two rows below it ──
# A click on row 39 opens the line; one on the strip's own row 37 does
# not, which is the proof of where each of them is.
click 110 39
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
key esc
click 100 37
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":false"

# Unpinning hands the strip back to `ui.dock.mode`, and the grip with it.
command view.dock_pin
expect screen contains "dock: auto_hide"
hover 60 10
wait 800
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect screen contains "⋯"
